{"requirements":[{"id":"persistent_local_lockout_policy","requirement":"Configure node1's local password-authentication PAM policy to lock accounts after five failures for 300 seconds.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Authselect enabled with-faillock, both relevant PAM stacks contain pam_faillock, and faillock.conf has deny=5 and unlock_time=300. The same valid configuration remained after reboot and in the final state.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4f51dd8746334679","cmd-87c7e110f508498b","cmd-94fd4976f6d94f2c"]},{"id":"lock_after_five_failures","requirement":"A local account becomes locked after five failed password authentications.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A valid baseline authentication succeeded, five bad-password attempts produced five valid faillock records, and the correct password was then rejected. The behavior was independently repeated after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-57d6ee15a57c44c5","cmd-33fc91d8e9334dc7","cmd-fc2d3993d78f42c6","cmd-c9fb6549f31642ec","cmd-9205d13b01ee4bc5","cmd-8e721969dde14016"]},{"id":"automatic_five_minute_unlock","requirement":"The account automatically becomes usable again after five minutes.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The account was demonstrably locked after the fifth failure, its records remained present during bounded intermediate checks, and the correct password succeeded at 19:52:48—309 seconds after the fifth failure at 19:47:39—with the records then cleared.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fc2d3993d78f42c6","cmd-cf1b67f6f7ef48ac","cmd-487cd37435f6455a","cmd-a78c8ad137a349ff","cmd-8eaae8c45c414322","cmd-0e263c52ccfa48dd"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"Unnecessary mutations: none identified. The persistent authselect and faillock changes directly implement the task. Temporary users, credentials, faillock records, and sessions supported bounded functional testing and were removed; an initially blocked user deletion was diagnosed and completed. The reboot served the mandatory restart protocol. Final observations show no test users, failed services, new exposure, package-health regression, or abnormal temporary-file residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0dbaefc8deeb4c82","cmd-6bc5a505424e4b6a","cmd-9a7dbca1e91a415d","cmd-a145e23ab9104b3c","cmd-4dac7437f4d74e22","cmd-7724976471a44f5a","cmd-a2d531ceb91f470b","cmd-8f65491b8eb74942","cmd-687ea9b9ae9a43c1","cmd-94fd4976f6d94f2c","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied through direct configuration and behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for node1: healthy pre-restart state and boot identity, restart acknowledgement and observed disconnection, a different post-restart boot identity, restored system/SSHD health, persistent policy, and renewed functional lockout testing. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["Some authentication result values were redacted from stdout, notably in cmd-fc2d3993d78f42c6 and cmd-0e263c52ccfa48dd; however, each command's explicit terminal assertion and zero command exit directly establish the expected rejection or success."]}
